ecided to name it as it is  and that is ganondorf's  second invasion after sending the hero  of time  back in time adult zelda stayed behind  and hyrule now without a hero and with  ganon sealed inside the sacred realm  started rebuilding and recovering from  the devastation left behind after  ganondorf's tyrannical rule  as the only surviving member of the  royal family princess zelda is crowned  and becomes queen  is married and eventually has offspring  thus re-establishing the royal family of  hyrule  this time of peace was short-lived  however as it wasn't long until  ganondorf somehow managed to break free  from the sacred realm and similar to the  child timeline despite being sealed for  all these countless years he is still in  possession of the triforce of power  zelda still holds the triforce of wisdom  and since the hero of time ceased to  exist the triforce of courage has been  split into pieces and hidden across the  kingdom  its whereabouts unknown ganondorf once  again set his eyes on obtaining the full  relic  starting with a piece of wisdom and came  eerily close to his goal  together with his army he invaded the  capital and was literally at the  kingdom's doorstep  when after a desperate plea for help  from hyrule's people none other than the  gods themselves suddenly decided to  interfere  after instructing hyrule's populace to  flee to the mountaintops hyrule's  creators let loose a torrential downpour  flooding the kingdom beneath a giant  body of water later known as the great  sea  this event is also known as the great  flood king daphne's no hanson hyrule  ganondorf and his army remained beneath  the waves sealed inside a bubble at the  bottom of the great sea  and due to the power of the master sword  even frozen in time  among those fleeing to the mountains was  princess zelda along with her royal  caretakers  and as you can see from this painting  hanging inside hyrule castle are the  literal  ancestors of what will later be tetra  and her crew of pirates  man genes sure are a powerful thing in  this universe  hundreds of years pass by since the  great flood and the events of the wind  waker sees the ever so persistent  ganondorf once again break free as he  makes his way to the world above the  waves to continue his hunt for the  triforce  which now lies partially in the hands of  tetra who again is  zelda's ancestor and partially in the  hands of the king of hyrule  and as mentioned before the triforce of  power still belongs to ganondorf and the  triforce of courage is still in pieces  and lies hidden around hyrule  similar to the downfall and child  timeline we will use ocarina of times  map of hyrule as a source for comparison  since this is how we last saw the  kingdom before the timeline split into  three obviously as far as changes go  well  i mean the entire kingdom has flooded  all that remains of the once prosperous  kingdom  are the peaks of the highest mountains  which now serve as small islands where  the descendants of hyrule's inhabitants  have lived their  lives in the centuries since let's take  a look at hyrule's races first  this time as this will come in handy  once we start dissecting the lay of the  land  obviously we have the hylians which as  stated before are the distant  descendants of the people who once lived  in hyrule before disaster struck as far  as settlements go the large majority of  them live on windfall island which is  now kinda like the new capital  and the smaller group are living on  outset island which is also where link  and his family grew up  these hylians live a more simple life as  farmers and fishermen whereas on  windfall we see more use of technology  such as a giant windmill which doubles  as a lighthouse  alchemy photography and explosives then  we have dorito which are confirmed to be  the descendants of the zora  at least in this timeline now you might  be asking yourself the very logical  question of  why on earth would an aquatic race like  the zora evolve into birds when there is  literally water  everywhere now shouldn't this be  paradise for them and the simple answer  is that unlike the zora from termina  which are clearly saltwater based  since they live in and around an ocean  the ones from ocarina of time are in all  probability used to a freshwater  environment  they live in and around a big river  after all and ocarina of times hyrule  features no oceans  now maybe the zora can adapt to other  water types  but that would require time to adjust  clearly a giant  rapid flood is too big and sudden of a  change and would give them no time to  adapt however we have seen them being  able to live on land for extended  periods of time  relative to zoro's domain death mountain  would have been the closest peak  so they fled from the domain to the  volcano and with the help of the dragon  spirit value evolved into the rito  the gorons are almost entirely gone as  beings made up of pure rock  obviously they aren't exactly made for  surviving in the water as they would  immediately sink to the bottom and drown  however there is still a small number of  them traveling the seas as merchants but  there is no goron capital to be found  anywhere  it could be that there are more of them  who survived the flood and are now  living somewhere else  but we'll get into that later next we  have the koroks who are shown to be the  pure and true form of the four spirits  formerly known as the kokiri in ocarina  of time they have continued to live with  the great deku tree who is confirmed to  be the very same deku tree as the sprout  we saw in ocarina of time after beating  the forest temple the reason we know  this is because he initially mistakes  this link for the hero of time  who as mentioned earlier no longer  exists in this timeline  and lastly we have the gerudo well one  of them anyway  as far as we know nothing remains of  ganondorf's people they are never seen  in this timeline and must mean that they  were either  exiled after ganondorf was sealed were  wiped out during ganondorf's second  invasion  or maybe were not able to make it to the  mountains in time to escape the great  flood  with that said it's time to look at the  map now obviously the large majority of  hyrule is no longer visible  with it being underwater and all and we  don't even know how far the great sea  spans outside the borders of ocarina of  times map but we can still look at a few  individual islands and make some  estimates now the sheer amount of  islands we see here might seem  surprising but hyrule has always been a  very mountainous land  just look at the landscape of twilight  princess as an example and you can see  just how many mountains surround the  kingdom  in almost every direction mountains and  large hills can be seen in the distance  to get some proper orientation let's  start with hyrule's former capital  which lies here directly below the tower  of the gods though it bears little to no  resemblance to the castle we saw in  ocarina of time i do believe that this  might still be the same location  the way the castle stands on this rock  formation with only one bridge leading  in and out strikes a strong resemblance  to the way ganon's castle was built  which of course collapsed in on itself  at the end of the game so it could be  that the hylians rebuilt the castle on  top of the remains an alternative would  be that they moved the castle to lake  hylia since as we can see the castle is  surrounded by a giant lake  connected to a river and as we can see  lake hylia did have a small island in  the middle of it  we can also see ganon's tower in the  distance and is actually relatively  close by  and by the looks of it could be on the  edge of gerudo valley or even inside the  desert itself  the bridge leading to the tower crosses  this canyon very similar to the grudo  canyon found in ocarina of time  more interestingly if we go out of  bounds in the final battle arena where  we fight ganondorf we can see that the  tower is surrounded by desert  of course this is something we wouldn't  be able to see during the fight itself  but this proves that the grudo desert  does still exist  and is where ganondorf built his new  tower preceding his second invasion  furthermore we see no trace of the  temple of time anywhere in this timeline  instead the master sword now resides in  a secret chamber in the basement of the  castle  hidden underneath a statue honoring the  hero of time likely built under the  command of zelda  after she sent him back in time to  commemorate all he had done for the  kingdom  we do find a set of ruins to the south  east of the castle  approximately where the temple of time  would have been if we were to assume  that the castle was built on top of the  remains of ganon's castle  so could these be the remains of the  holy site and these other ruins in front  of the castle the remnants of castle  town  it's hard to say for sure but it's an  interesting thought nonetheless  regardless the temple of time is  obviously no longer around  either the hylians took it down after  ganondorf was sealed in order to get rid  of the entrance to the sacred realm  which the temple originally was  or it may have been destroyed during  ganon's second invasion after he broke  free from the sacred realm  whatever the case may be the master  sword had long since been moved to the  secret room in the castle's basement and  king  daphnis even comments on how ganondorf  never even knew about the existence of  this chamber  so moving the sword here seems to have  been the right call aside from being the  new resting place of the legendary blade  the chamber also serves as sort of a  memorial to the events of ocarina of  time it even depicts the original six  sages on the stained glass windows  now that we know where the original  capital lies we can start looking at  some of the islands and see if we can  find some original landmarks in the  world above  i won't be covering every island of  course as we would be here all week  besides most islands are clearly just  random previously unnamed mountain peaks  and nothing more  nothing we could cross-reference with  ocarina of times map but when we compare  the map of the wind waker to ocarina we  do see some familiar faces  death mountain has always been to the  northeast of the castle and on the great  sea  northeast of the tower of the gods we  find dragon roost island here it goes  without saying that this is most likely  the very same volcano death mountain has  historically always been the highest  peak in hyrule  and here too it stands as the tallest  island around aside from the tower of  the gods though that one is clearly  man-made we do see one additional  volcanic island but this one is very  small and so close to dragon roost that  it is likely an extension of the death  mountain region  ever since skyward sword we've seen that  there are other peaks surrounding the  volcano which also spew out smoke or  even lava  so the location definitely matches in  relation to the castle  the name change to dragon roost island  is also quite logical since we  already established in part one that the  name death mountain was given to the  volcano by the gorons who for many  millennia after skyward sword made their  home here  after the flood the gorons disappeared  from the volcano and now dorito formerly  known as the zora have been living here  for the past centuries alongside their  dragon deity  so they simply renamed it to dragon  roost windfall island is an interesting  one  it shares a similar soundtrack as  kakrico village but it's obvious that  the two villages are not the same  kakariko would have been located here  close to death mountain  however it is possible that the  inhabitants of windfall are descendants  of the people from kakariko the only  thing that doesn't make sense is the  location  since the village was so close to death  mountain you would think that this was  the most  logical escape option when the great  flood happened of course we don't know  how much time the people of hyrule were  given to evacuate before the water  started rising but perhaps the volcanic  environment of death mountain was simply  too dangerous and uninhabitable for the  highlands of kakariko  and instead they set off to a different  mountain to the northwest of the capital  alternatively maybe they did initially  flee to death mountain but again since  the environment wasn't suitable they  later sailed from dragon roost to  windfall and established their new town  here kakariko has historically been tied  to the shika  in ocarina of time it was originally a  shika village built by them  but because most of them were wiped out  during the hyrulian civil war the  village became predominantly occupied by  hylians and although the chica are  completely gone in this timeline and  are never seen again we do find one clue  of their heritage on windfall mrs mary  the teacher on windfall has what seems  like a stylistic depiction of a chica  eye on her outfit  this could mean that one or more  inhabitants of windfall have chica  ancestry or at the very least that a  part of their culture was preserved by  the hylians who fled to windfall since  the chica were already close to extinct  in ocarina of time  so in a way windfall and kakariko could  actually be connected in terms of their  culture and ancestry but geologically  they are completely separate from one  another next we have the forest haven  which matches with the location the  kokiri forest and lost woods would have  been located in relative to hyrule's  capital in ocarina  of time that is to say to the southeast  of the castle  it's not exactly clear how the forest  and deku tree came to exist on this  mountain peak since  i don't remember any big mountains in  and around the forest in ocarina of time  but then again the deku tree is a spirit  guardian  i guess he could have elevated the land  around him or grown a giant wooden  cocoon around it  i mean it is literally a tree within a  tree  so anything is possible when spirits are  involved and  honestly that's about it in terms of  islands we can use for reference  obviously looking for a lake or river  inside an ocean would be impossible so  lake hylia and the old zorus domain are  lost forever  and other places like london ranch and  the aforementioned kakariko village  would have also been completely  submerged  and none of them are visible from the  underwater hyrule castle either but if  hyrule castle was indeed still in the  same general area  as it was in ocarina of time they would  have been located somewhere around here  and although we do see the desert in the  out of bounds section  i showed earlier on the great sea we  don't really see anything familiar from  that province though i do find it poetic  that ganondorf's home base on the great  sea  is the forsaken fortress which is  approximately where the desert would  have been located to the west of the  capital  all the other islands even the ones  which play a pretty big role like outset  and great fish isle don't seem to have  any correlation with anything we would  be able to find in ocarina of time as  stated before they would have been  located on unnamed or even unseen  mountain peak somewhere  at the end of the wind waker the  underwater void which the old kingdom of  hyrule has resided in for centuries  finally collapses in on itself and the  last remains finally washed away  and buried beneath the waves officially  ending the existence of the kingdom  as we know it and that wraps up the wind  waker and we can finally move on to  phantom hourglass we will largely skip  over this game since it has  little to no relation to hyrule the  entire adventure takes place in a world  called the realm of the ocean king  because i only played this game once  a long time ago i initially thought this  was just a location outside the borders  of the great sea from the wind waker  somewhere but it is  actually another parallel dimension one  which link and tetra access through a  portal while aboard a mysterious ghost  ship while the rest of the crew stays  behind  and yes these are still the same  characters from the previous game and  only takes place a short time after the  events of the wind waker we know for a  fact that this  is a parallel world we can clearly see  the portal  time also moves differently between the  two dimensions since when the duo  returns to their own world they are  surprised to hear from the crew that  only about 10 minutes has passed for  them  i also quickly have to mention the  existence of this graph i only recently  discovered in hyrule encyclopedia i know  the canonicity of encyclopedia  is often questioned it does provide some  very cool tidbits of information  but it also makes some claims which fans  have debated or even flat out debunked  this graph  also depicts the realm of the ocean king  as a parallel world but i do find the  chart itself  a bit odd for instance i have no idea  why they chose to categorize these  worlds as  either parallel worlds or kingdoms  because some can be both  after all lorule is listed as a kingdom  but it's also clearly a different  dimension  we travel to it using rifts or portals  the same thing goes for labranow which  according to this chart is also a  parallel world but it's also  unmistakably a kingdom ruled over by  queen ambi i think it would have been  better to just classify them as  either parallel or non-parallel or  something oh and  by the way in part two about the  downfall timeline i stated that labrun  and holodrum are likely on the same  physical plane as hyrule but apparently  they are not in some ways this does make  sense seeing as link is transported here  by the triforce but it also raises some  questions considering that zelda and her  nurse made empire visit these worlds as  well either before  or after link arrives there i don't know  maybe portal travel was just  everyday business in hyrule but i  digress the realm of the ocean king is  structured very similar to that of the  great sea  a vast body of water with small islands  scattered across  hence my initial confusion that this was  on the same physical plane  in terms of races we once again find the  hylians like lineback and jolene  the anuki a brand new eskimo or inuit  type of race  the yuk also new to the series and who  are on bad terms with the anuki due to a  misunderstanding and interestingly  enough the gorons who have their own  island here  it's not clear if these are related to  the gorons from ocarina of time or the  few merchants we saw in the wind waker  but if they are it could be that the  majority of them fled to this dimension  during or after the great flood  not that this dimension is any better i  mean it's still a vast ocean but  oh well other than that there isn't  really much to say as  again this land has nothing to do with  hyrule or even the land surrounding it  it exists on a separate plane of  existence  it has its own locations and even its  own deity who watches over the land a  giant whale called oshas who has a lot  in common with the windfish from link's  awakening and i believe belongs to the  same type of leviathan deities  last up we have spirit tracks again this  game doesn't take place in hyrule  well technically anyway keep in mind at  the end of the wind waker the kingdom  was submerged for good however the  islands above the water still exist  so technically hyrule isn't completely  gone the kingdom is but places like  outset  windfall forest haven and dragon roost  are still there  however spirit tracks takes place on a  completely new continent one that  already existed for  who knows how long at some point in time  link tetra and the crew discovered this  new continent and their descendants  would go on to establish an entirely new  kingdom  this kingdom is often referred to as new  hyrule but other than the bloodline of  princess zelda it has no relation to the  original hyrule whatsoever  the continent itself isn't even called  hyrule only the kingdom does  the land is actually referred to as the  land of spirits of good  it even has its own history of events  preceding the time when the hylians  first landed here and established their  kingdom like the battle between the  spirit beings known as the lokomo and  the ancient demon by the name of maladus  although many characters we see in  spirit tracks have some very strong  resemblances to those from the wind  waker and phantom hourglass  nico is actually the only original  founder of new hyrule who is still alive  as far as we know everyone else  including link and zelda are descendants  seeing as how this is a completely new  continent it has very little impact on  the history of the kingdom of hyrule  in fact since this is the last game it  actually marks the end of its history  an old kingdom replaced by a brand new  one in faraway lands  we do see some of those good old hylian  naming traditions pop up once again  though  we have the obvious ones like hyrule  castle and hyrule field but also the  lost woods and kokiri village  there's no lake hylia and although there  is a volcano it isn't called death  mountain  what we do find aside from the hylians  are gorons who have apparently  also managed to make their way to this  new continent at some point  or already lived here before i don't  know  we do find zora as well though these are  the hostile kind akin to the ones we saw  in a link to the past  so probably not related to the rito from  the wind waker in any way the anuki also  make a return in this game and lastly we  have the lokomo who are more or less  divine beings similar to the sages  and yeah that pretty much sums up spirit  tracks as i said at the beginning of the  video the adult timeline feels like the  most consistent  and well-constructed sequence of events  three adventures which all follow up on  one another in a way that makes sense  chronologically a continuous voyage that  starts off with an ancient  legendary kingdom on its last legs and  is finally wiped from existence when its  purpose is fulfilled  in the end we see our heroes set sail  towards the horizon and  unknown lands in hopes of finding a new  future phantom hourglass serves as sort  of a side adventure  an unknown world in peril which they  happened to stumble upon on their  travels  after saving this world the same heroes  continued their search  until after years of traversing the vast  seas they finally find a new continent  where they establish a new kingdom where  their descendants will live on  and to pay homage to their lineage they  continue the naming tradition of hyrule  to pay tribute to the land which they  once originated from  it actually feels planned each game  picks up where the other one left off  we even hear a train whistle and the  sound of wheels on a track at the end of  phantom hourglass  proving that they already knew and  hinted at what the next installment was  going to be  [Music]  [Applause]  and with that we have reached the end of  the evolution of hyrule  for now at least i will eventually do  one final episode on breath of the wild  hyrule however it feels best if we wait  until after breath dwell 2 has come and  gone  as of right now we don't even know where  breath wild falls on the timeline hence  we have nothing to compare it to  we don't even know which version of  hyrule preceded this hyrule  or if it will even get a definitive  placement but the sequel could  potentially provide more information or  even totally explain  everything so until then i will keep  this series on hold for the time being  i hope you enjoyed this deep dive into  hyrule's history and geography  and thank you for joining me on this  journey and finally a big thanks to all  of my amazing patreon supporters and  channel members  we have two new faces joining the maze  so say hello to lux pro  and kyle thank you both so much for your  generosity  you guys are the best and that wraps up  the video i will see you in the next one  this is don  signing off and have a good one  [Music]  you

